l_use if needed, save answers? save_answer counts as separate tools but not model requests. Hmm, \"requests_left\":3 counts model requests presumably (my actions). Actually request_number 37, max 40 → 3 remaining actions total. Tight.\n\nSo I must do it in ~2-3 actions: one for remaining evidence recall, then one big action with all notes + save_answers + save_sections + submit_report + final_answer.\n\nBut rules: \"After all pages and all five latest notes have appeared together in a later request, call submit_report\". So submit must be in an action after notes. That's 3 actions: recall, notes, submit. Very tight but feasible.\n\nCan I combine recall of pending evidence in same action as notes? Notes need content from those pages. Risky without seeing text.\n\nAlternative: I know this paper somewhat. But quotes must be exact from pages. I need delivered evidence text.\n\nLet me do action 1: recall the six pending ids (tool allows batching). Then hopefully delivery happens in this response... Actually recall returns queued; delivery occurs after the action (in next feedback). So action 2 shows text; then action 2 can also write notes? No—I only see text after action 1 completes. So action 2 writes notes, action 3 submit. That's exactly 3.\n\nAlternatively submit_report+final_answer in action 3. Yes.\n\nRisk: if delivery of 6 pages in one recall exceeds batch limits. Earlier recall of 8 delivered 2 pages. Ugh. 6 pages might deliver partially.\n\nBetter: recall fewer critical pages. Which pages? multi_agent (CAMEL, Generative Agents) probably around page 30-35. outlook Table 4 near page 45-50. I don't know ids for those pages. The pending list: ev-b8db09 (15), ev-ced75d (?), ev-9317b0 (?), ev-6297cb (?), ev-562f05 (?), ev-f5fab5 (?), ev-e5b9499 (?), ev-7f4d5e (?) — total queued 40, so I can't list all.\n\nHmm, I could use recall with a list of ids I pick... but I don't know locators for unqueued. I could call read_pdf again for specific pages — but that's a model action too, and counts. Actually reading via read_pdf tool returns pages directly in result! That's better: read_pdf(30,35) would return content in the tool result within the same... no, results come back after my action ends too.\n\nHmm. The tool result delivery happens after my action. So each action can gather info.\n\nGiven 3 actions left: \nAction 1: read_pdf(28, 36) and read_pdf(44,52)? Each read_pdf returns pages immediately in the feedback. Let's try one call read_pdf(1,52)? That was done. Better to read specific ranges: multi_agent content and outlook content. Let me guess: CAMEL is discussed in section on multi-agent society, maybe pages 30-33. Table 4 research agenda likely page 48-50.\n\nAction 1: read_pdf(29, 34) plus recall ids? I can call multiple tools in one action? The instruction says only one fenced Python block; I can call multiple functions in the block and print. Yes, group independent operations.\n\nSo action 1: \n- r1 = read_pdf(28,35)\n- r2 = read_pdf(45,52)\n- print relevant excerpts.\n\nBut read_pdf returns dict with pages; printing all pages too long. I can print only pages containing keywords like 'CAMEL', 'Generative Agents', 'Table 4'.\n\nGood. Then action 2: write notes (5), save answers/sections, then action 3: submit + final_answer.\n\nWait: submit requires notes to appear together in a later request. Notes written in action 2; action 3 submit — the notes event is included in the context of action 3? The plan states that's fine.\n\nAlso need reasoning note (Tree of Thoughts controllers) — that's on a reasoning page ~9-11. Include read_pdf(7,12) in action 1.\n\nLet's do it."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8372,"completion_tokens":1345,"total_tokens":9717,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4352},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1193},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4352,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":4020},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}